<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iyasu II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1723–1755</span> · Also known as Iyasu II of Ethiopia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iyasu II was Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> from 1730 to 1755, ruling for much of his reign under the regency of his mother, Empress Mentewab. His court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gondar">Gondar</a> was a centre of building and painting. In 1744 he led a large invasion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/funj-sultanate-of-sennar">Funj Sultanate of Sennar</a>, which ended in defeat on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dinder-river">Dinder River</a>. His death was followed by the decline of imperial authority.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iyasu-ii.jpg" alt="Iyasu II" width="320" height="364" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unnamed · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iyasu_II_of_Ethiopia_and_Mentewab.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
